cff-version: 1.2.0

title: "qBTC: A Post-Quantum Bitcoin Protocol"

version: 0.2.0

type: software

license: MIT

date-released: "2025-04-19"

abstract: >-
  qBTC is a complete reimplementation of the Bitcoin protocol for the
  post-quantum era. It replaces all Shor-vulnerable cryptographic
  primitives with NIST-standardized post-quantum algorithms (ML-DSA-65,
  SLH-DSA, ML-KEM-1024) and all Grover-vulnerable hashes with SHA3-256.
  The protocol features a three-phase hybrid consensus mechanism
  (QPoW → QPoW+PoS → PoS) with a 64-bit nonce that neutralizes Grover's
  quadratic speedup. Reference implementation in Python 3.12+ with liboqs.

message: >-
  If you use this software in your research, please cite it using the
  metadata in this file. A DOI is available via Zenodo.

